# E10 layer 1 of 3, carried here from the canary repository, and for the same reason.
#
# `* -text` turns OFF git's line-ending translation for every file in this repository.
# It is not a style preference. This console stores RECEIVED data: run folders as an
# emitter wrote them, and the verifier's reports over those bytes. A checkout that
# rewrote one byte of a receipt would destroy the only thing the receipt is for, and it
# would do it silently and with a green exit code, because from git's point of view it
# was being helpful.
#
# The other two layers live where they always do: exclusion lists in pyproject.toml keep
# every formatter, linter and auto-fixer out of the received-data paths, and digest tests
# assume both earlier layers have already failed and ask the only question that survives
# that assumption -- are the bytes still the bytes?
#
# A preventive control that cannot be observed failing is not a control.
* -text
